WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.040
My Mom used to tell me all the time...

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.430
About the Hero of Center City...

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.770
There was a fire in that coal mine 
13 years ago... A terrible accident.

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:59.380
A great number of people working inside 
became trapped with no way out.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.090
When the people caught up in the fire 
started giving up and losing the will to live,

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.200
a single coal miner stood up.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.900
He said, "Don't give up!"

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.720
He took the other miners and 
ran into an old passage.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.160
But their final hope of escape 
was blocked by piles of rubble.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.480
With the flames bearing down on them, 
the coal miners didn't give up.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.440
Even so...

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.490
Hey!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.260
That coal miner gave everything 
he had to save everyone.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.810
That was...

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.530
...my father.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.920
Man, way to be all gloomy 
right in the morning.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:25.990
I couldn't protect him.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.100
I couldn't protect him like Dad did.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.510
If I was a hero like Dad...

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.170
Psy wouldn't have been injured like that...

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.800
What the hell are you talking about?

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.510
That guy ain't no hero in the first place!

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.760
Dad is a hero who protected 
everyone in Center City!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.150
That worthless idiot is no hero!

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.320
He's a hero!

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.600
Then tell me.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.000
What is a hero?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.980
Listen, Heroman...

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.280
Even before I met you, I 
always admired heroes...

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.530
Because I was weak, and a coward...

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.500
And Dad was a great man, strong and 
reliable... Everyone could count on him.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.920
I wanted to be a hero like him.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.020
But I don't remember much about Dad.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.460
A hero... huh?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.600
What's the matter, Joey? Did 
you get picked on again?

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:04.140
You Dad was a hero, and he'd 
never cry, no matter what.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.920
So you shouldn't cry so easily, Joey.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.420
See?

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.630
Don't worry about it, Joey.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:24.500
I'll all healed up. They said 
I'll be discharged tomorrow.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.660
Really?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:26.740
Yeah!

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:31.780
And besides, I got hurt 
because of my own weakness.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.690
It's not your fault.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:35.980
But...

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.190
I wanted to protect you.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.210
Yeah, that's it! That's what's important.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.980
That's exactly why you're my hero!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.420
Hero... huh?

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.310
A hero, you ask?

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:56.050
You should know a lot about heroes, right?

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.650
M-Me?

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.420
Yeah, obviously.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.320
H-How did you know?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.050
About Heroma-

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.830
What are you talking about?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.670
Brian Jones! He's the hero of Center City!

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:10.990
Brian?

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.760
Oh, that name brings back memories.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.390
You knew him?

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.940
Of course! Ain't no one that doesn't 
who worked in the coal mines.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.880
I'm his son, Joseph!

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.200
Amazing! You're Brian and Catherine's kid?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.200
I see... My, you've grown.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:38.080
That guy was always thinking about 
helping his friends over himself.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.090
And that's the reason it happened...

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.290
He had a habit of tapping his head...

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:49.220
"I'm gonna protect them," he'd say...

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.910
There's no doubting it! He's our hero!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.720
Thank you!

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.890
See you tomorrow!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:03.540
Dad was a hero! For real!

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.620
Joey!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.260
Lina!

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.450
Why are you here?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.060
Um, it's just...

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.470
I want to ask...

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.890
Hey, listen!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.370
My dad really was a hero!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.660
The stories Mom used to tell me were true!

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.430
Oh, I see...

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.420
Good for you, then...

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.650
I've got to hurry and tell my sister!

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:33.590
Later!

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.020
Wait, Joey...

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.600
Sis! Hey, Sis!

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.110
What?

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.460
Dad really was a hero!

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.840
That's what everyone said!

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.370
So what?

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.470
It doesn't matter what other people say.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:58.620
Why are you saying things like that?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.100
Why do you say that about Dad?

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:05.590
Oh yeah... You don't remember 
much about him, do you?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:08.740
Why?

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.710
Why do you say such mean things about Dad?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.880
Will you shut up? I've told you already.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.720
That guy ain't no hero!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.730
He's just a good-for-nothing!

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.060
Sis...

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.100
You don't understand, Sis!

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.480
What's the matter?

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:40.660
It's nothing.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.310
I know more about him than anyone...

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.400
Who is it?

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:40.360
Will?

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.100
Stay there.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:49.100
I don't want you to see me like this.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.760
Don't go away anywhere again!

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.200
How are mother and father?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.080
They're always worrying about you!

00:09:58.620 --> 00:09:59.840
Isn't that obvious?

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.650
And not just our parents... 
Everyone at school, too!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.560
It didn't seem that way to me.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.070
I met Joey.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:11.560
Joey?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.370
He didn't say anything?

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.800
True... There's no way he could 
tell you that we clashed...

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:19.830
No way...

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.810
Don't involve yourself with him anymore.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.390
Do you understand?

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:25.990
Will...

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.420
Lina.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.630
What is it?

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.560
I came today to say goodbye.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.340
I do not think we will see each other again.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.510
Will!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.150
Take care of our parents.

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:41.940
Wait, Will!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:52.580
Lina!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.000
Father...

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.370
What's the matter, Lina?

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.700
Did something happen at school?

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.760
It's about my brother...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:11.300
I thought I told you not to concern 
yourself with Will any longer.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:13.030
But, Father...

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.750
Understand, Lina?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.610
Will is dead!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.410
No!

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.330
He's dead!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.170
No!

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.470
My brother is not dead!

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:24.650
Hey, Lina!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.950
Where do you think you're going?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.230
I'm hungry...

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:45.960
Hey, Heroman... Why do you think my 
sister says such mean things about Dad?

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:51.580
Everyone sings his praises... 
Everyone except her...

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.980
What is a hero, anyway?

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.340
A true hero...

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.850
Maybe I'll try asking.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.290
I knew you'd be here.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.150
Sis...

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:51.160
You never change.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.590
Every time anything happens 
you come here to tell them.

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:56.670
How about actually moving on, for a change?

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.120
So, you found the answer?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.570
About what a hero really is?

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.470
Before that... Tell me about Dad.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.640
Why is it that you say Dad isn't a hero?

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.480
Because he did something 
I just can't forgive.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.710
He lied to me.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:25.470
On that day, he left the 
house like he always did.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.310
He promised that he'd be back by 6.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.270
That was the last time I ever saw him.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:13.460
After who knows how many days, 
I finally figured it out.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.950
He was never coming back.

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:22.370
He forgot the promise he made me.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:27.820
Yeah, he may be a hero that saved 
a bunch of people's lives...

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.540
Everyone was thankful to 
him, and praised him...

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.680
But who cares about that?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.390
What about the family he left behind?

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:44.470
Mom was proud of Dad.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:47.110
She never said anything 
bad about him like you.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.240
Did you ever see Mom cry?

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.670
She never showed her tears to anyone.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:15:00.340
No matter how sad she was...
No matter how much in pain she was...

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:02.610
She was always smiling.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:05.890
But...

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.290
But I know she must have 
been crying in secret...

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:15.430
All alone, so that we wouldn't see...

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.950
Crying out, "If only he was still here..."

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:23.120
She pushed herself for us... She forced herself...

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.980
And before we knew it, she died...

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.280
Sis...

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:33.490
You see...

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:38.260
Even if everyone around the world looks 
up to him, and praised what he did...

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.410
I'd rather...

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.230
...he'd stayed by our side.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:53.430
He acted all cool and tried too hard 
to be a hero... That's why he died.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.320
It's funny, you know?

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:02.620
All that's left for his family 
is that little dirty helmet.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:10.810
He'd tap his head, and say 
"I'm gonna protect them..."

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:30.890
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.090
Just come!

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.970
I heard that Dad had a 
habit of tapping his head.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.980
He never did anything like that at home...

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:55.370
I bet Dad thought about his family 
a lot more than you think, Sis.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.300
"I'm gonna protect them."

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.950
In other words...

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.800
That's what it was.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:32.010
You're the reason I get up everyday!

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.910
We were always with him.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.340
See?

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:57.420
Dad... You idiot...

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.860
Will you tell me where Lina is?

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.970
I've already searched everywhere around here!

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.750
But, I can't find her anywhere!

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:23.570
Lina?

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.140
<i>Hello?</i>

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.230
Lina, are you okay?

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:46.700
<i>Honestly... No, I'm not really okay.</i>

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.220
Where are you now?

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.850
Everyone's worried about you!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.500
<i>What do mean, everyone?</i>

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.960
Hey Lina, where are you? Come home imme-

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.820
Lina! Hey, Lina!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.570
Oh, my... This is trouble.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.130
Um...

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.120
I'll go look for her.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.310
Joey...

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.250
How did you know I was here?

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:45.800
I heard the sound of waves over 
the phone, so I figured...

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:50.640
Did you have a fight with your father?

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.870
I had a fight with my sister about Dad.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.040
With your sister?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.600
Dad died when I was still little.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:07.130
So, I don't remember very 
much about him at all.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.850
And, well...

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:19.990
But, thanks to that, my sister and I feel 
closer to him now than we did before.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:24.950
Sorry... I didn't mean to bother you...

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.620
No, no!

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.310
That's not what I was trying to say.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:30.890
It's...

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.730
How should I put this?

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.740
I understand.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:42.380
I'm...

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.340
I'm not going to waver anymore.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:50.920
I can do this!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:56.850
Joey?

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:00.860
This is...

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:16.840
I bet that a new ability 
has awakened in Heroman.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:22.270
So, what about you, Lina?

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.550
Didn't you have something you 
wanted to talk with me about?

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:27.450
Yeah...

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:29.760
I did...

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.910
Don't involve yourself with him any longer.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.490
Lina?

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:41.620
Joey!

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:44.590
Um...

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.100
Professor Denton?

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:51.990
Hello?

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:54.160
Yes.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.930
Okay...

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:00.730
Yes.

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:03.800
Professor Denton wanted to 
know if you were here with me.

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.210
Hello?

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.350
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:55.210
I won't waver any longer!

00:23:55.210 --> 00:23:57.660
That's why I'm going to go, and finish this!

00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:00.150
"Everything is connected."

00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:02.400
That's what Hughes said in a hushed voice...

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:05.780
The series of events that seemed 
isolated at first glance...

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:09.000
